 2. 💡 &quot;Simplify&quot;: Killing workplace bloat 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Cover: Crown Currency

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Our bestseller " Smart Brevity " gave companies a common language and skill set to simplify communications. A week from today, Jim, Roy, and I will be out with " Simplify : Do 50% More with 50% Less," which gives you tools to kill complexity so you can be happier and more productive.

 Why it matters: We're hearing from lots of overwhelmed leaders trying to simplify how their organizations operate. But it's hard to get everyone aligned to make it happen. And AI turns out to be a massive complexity-generation machine, drowning us in decks and dashboards.

 Your solution: "Simplify." Case in point: Roy ran across a podcast featuring psychologist Ron Friedman, author of " Superteams ," who has studied how to cut through the bloat of meetings and messages to give you more time for work that matters. Among his findings that match the "Simplify" mindset:

 The average office worker spends 18 hours a week in meetings and 11 hours digging through messages. That's 73% of the week — leaving just over one day a week for real work. High-performing organizations ruthlessly cut back on standing meetings, stand-ups and check-ins. "Meetings are a last resort, not a default," he says. Friedman recommends meeting-free days, when no one is expected to respond to in-the-moment messages. He calls these "Get Things Done Days." Want more productivity power tools? "Simplify" will help you, and everyone in your company, do the right work ... not more work.

