 4. 🗳️ Exclusive poll: GOP&#x27;s Latino gains fade 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Hart Research/TelevisaUnivision. Table: Russell Contreras/Axios Democrats have gained sharply with Latino voters in some of the country's most competitive House districts since 2024, Axios' Russell Contreras writes from a new Hart Research/TelevisaUnivision poll. 

 Democrats are gaining ground with Latino voters across a survey of 17 competitive House districts, opening a 58%-35% lead on the generic congressional ballot. That 23-point margin is double the 11-point edge Kamala Harris held over Trump in the same sample's self-reported 2024 vote. The intrigue: 11% of Latino voters who say they backed Trump in 2024 now support Democratic congressional candidates.

