 7. 👢 Republicans roll into Dallas 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Mark Felix/Bloomberg via Getty Images More than 100 Republican House members and candidates are expected at the American Airlines Center in Dallas for the party's first-ever midterm convention tomorrow and Thursday, running for six hours each night, 4-10 p.m. ET. (with competition from NFL season openers).

 Lots of lawmakers in competitive races are taking a pass or hedging about their plans. Organizers have scheduled 50+ speakers or presentations each night, with many of the slots kept brief for easy online sharing. Everyday Americans, including former Democrats, will take turns onstage talking about how they've benefited from Trump policies.

 President Trump will speak each night. Vice President JD Vance will keynote Thursday. 📺 C-SPAN plans gavel-to-gavel coverage, and C-SPAN2 will be on the campaign trail with Democrats.

